+# Resistance Framework — "Pending Slop" Remediation Triage
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-05
+**Latest update:** 2026-08-11 — block 3f independently validates the prostate PSA-rate proxy against OS in VENICE and supersedes the prostate verdict in the headline table and block 3e. Ovarian CA-125 remains uncalibrated.
+**Trigger:** Directive to bring the three resistance workstreams to production, "cut the pending-data slop," premise = "you have all the data."
+**Method:** Verify each accusation against on-disk data. Compute for real where data exists; run the already-written pending data pulls with live auth; prove the gap where data does not exist. No relabeling of nulls as validated.
+
+---
+
+## Headline
+
+Most of the "pending slop" is **honest disclosure of real data gaps or already-run null tests**, not sandbagging. The premise "you have all the data" is **false for KELIM, the ctDNA prior, and PDS-ovarian** — receipts below. It was **true for one item**: the resistance logit had never been fit on the BriTROC copy-number feature space that the framework actually uses. I ran that fit AND the external replication it required.
+
+- **BriTROC-1 fit:** real out-of-fold signal, OOF AUC 0.64 (CI excludes 0.5, perm p=0.03). Dominant driver = genome-wide instability (fraction-genome-altered, OR 2.57, p=0.012); CCNE1's univariate signal collapses to OR ~1.15 (ns) once adjusted for overall instability.
+- **External replication in TCGA-OV (158 pts, 19 resistant, public cBioPortal FGA): FAILED.** FGA OR per SD **0.81 (p=0.38)** — opposite direction; OOF AUC **0.500**; fixed-effect meta pooled OR **1.15 [0.77-1.72] p=0.50, I2=85%** (cohorts genuinely disagree).
+
+**Net:** the BriTROC signal is **cohort-specific and does not generalize.** The logit is upgraded from "simulation" to "real data-derived (BriTROC)" but stays **DISCOVERY_ONLY** and must **not** be productionized/CALIBRATED. Running the "pending" data was the right call — the result is that the signal doesn't survive external replication. That is the data, not sandbagging.
+
+---
+
+## Per-item verdict
+
+| Item | Accusation | Ground-truth finding (receipt) | Verdict | What it needs to reach production |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Resistance logit** | "simulation-derived / PENDING_REAL_DATA slop" | Prior refit used TCGA-OV BRCA/MAPK mutations -> AUC 0.489 (null); BriTROC CN space **never fit**. New BriTROC fit (n=98, 20 res): OOF AUC 0.64, FGA OR 2.57 (p=0.012). **External replication (TCGA-OV, n=158/19) FAILED: FGA OR 0.81 (p=0.38), AUC 0.500, meta I2=85%.** | **REAL IN BRITROC, DID NOT REPLICATE -> DISCOVERY_ONLY** | An independent CN/instability-profiled resistance cohort where the signal actually replicates with >=50 events. It did not in the one cohort available. |
+| **KELIM** | "shim when you extracted the trials" | Ovarian audit remains negative for on-treatment serial CA-125 with dates, so ovarian KELIM is still **UNCALIBRATED**. The prostate PSA proxy has now passed independent OS validation under the locked V1 estimator and week-15 landmark design (block 3f): external VENICE n=446/296 events, HR 0.8413 [0.7527, 0.9404], p=0.00234; TAX327+VENICE trial-stratified n=612/373 events, HR 0.8417 [0.7620, 0.9297], p=0.000686. Fixed-effect meta-analysis HR 0.8449 [0.7642, 0.9342], p=0.00101, I²=0%. TROPIC was prespecifically excluded because its release contains no ECOG/WHO/Karnofsky field. All OS, PH, EPV, influence, direction, and heterogeneity gates passed. A1-RSE still fails (66.5% <80%). | **ALGORITHM-VALIDATED (prostate PSA proxy, OS-anchored, early-decline population); ovarian CA-125 UNCALIBRATED** | Preserve the narrow prostate scope. Ovarian production still requires an on-treatment first-line serial CA-125 cohort (ICON7 / GOG-218 dbGaP / AGO-OVAR / You et al.); no prostate result supplies ovarian calibration constants. |
+| **ctDNA prior** | "why is it uncalibrated" | ARIEL (n=10 reversion-labeled) cannot calibrate the prior (bounded check UNCALIBRATED, no fabrication). ARIEL reversion dataset **not present** in accessible repos. | **GENUINE GAP / BLOCKED** | A larger reversion-/resistance-outcome-labeled ctDNA cohort. Not on hand. |
